// Decision line 3, a field template reached under parents on two
// domains (Birth, Run).
//
// `Parent`'s field default `Leaf { }` is one template however many
// `Parent` literals build it, and two do: `App`'s run() on main and
// `Worker`'s run() on pool `side`. Each Leaf is built inline in its own
// Parent's params, on that Parent's thread, so the template's birth and
// run claim the set of the two domains, and each occurrence runs on one
// of them; neither parent's domain alone is the template's. (The
// reviewer's program, with a body in Leaf's run(): an empty one is
// never called.) On `side` the Leaf's run() is posted to the worker
// running Worker's run(), behind the teardown of the Parent statement,
// which cancels it before it starts (line 19); on main it runs.
//
// Expected terminal outcome: one Leaf born on each parent's domain,
// judged by the harness from the trace: `born-on-each-parents-domain`.

locus Leaf { run() { println("ev leaf-run"); } }
locus Parent { params { leaf: Leaf = Leaf { }; } }
locus Worker { run() { Parent { }; } }
main locus App {
    params { worker: Worker = Worker { }; }
    placement { worker: cooperative(pool = side); }
    run() { Parent { }; }
}
fn main() { App { }; }
